  "solution": "For the quadratic equation  \n\\[\n3x^2-7x-8=0,\n\\]\nthe roots are\n\\[\nx=\\frac{7\\pm \\sqrt{(-7)^2-4(3)(-8)}}{2(3)}\n=\\frac{7\\pm \\sqrt{49+96}}{6}\n=\\frac{7\\pm \\sqrt{145}}{6}.\n\\]\n\nThe positive difference between the roots is\n\\[\n\\frac{7+\\sqrt{145}}{6}-\\frac{7-\\sqrt{145}}{6}\n=\\frac{2\\sqrt{145}}{6}\n=\\frac{\\sqrt{145}}{3}.\n\\]\n\nThus \\(m=145\\) and \\(n=3\\). Since \\(145=5\\cdot 29\\) is squarefree,\n\\[\nm+n=145+3=148.\n\\]\n\nThe answer is 148.",
